SUMMARY: The Face is a Landscape
DESCRIPTION:"The Face is a Landscape" is a visual arts exhibition by Toro
 nto artist Angela Julian. The large body of art features colorful works d
 one in Portraiture. The show is comprised of drawings and paintings creat
 ed in a highly-detailed contemporary style. She explores painterly and dr
 awn techniques in both wet and dry mediums. The faces are designed using 
 many layers of blended line-work\, impressions\, and cross-hatchings. She
  uses very fine brushes and drawing instruments to achieve these micro-te
 chniques that makeup the broader whole of the picture. The works are loca
 ted in the Star Gallery and fill up the room from floor to ceiling. The s
 ubjects of each portrait are all well-known authors\, writers\, or philos
 ophers by nature. Angela is penning her first book series in the high-fan
 tasy genre\, she has included portraits in the show based on writers that
  had a direct impact on her as a reader and aspiring author. The exhibiti
 on is largely a homage to those writers and thinkers who influenced her.\
 n\n\nThe Star Gallery is located at 918 Bathurst Arts & Culture Center in
  the Annex neighborhood (Bloor / Bathurst area). The center is a historic
  building in Toronto and was formerly a Buddhist Temple before it became 
 a venue for Arts and Culture. It has an in-house audience that ranges fro
 m both broad to local. With many disappearing gallery spaces in Toronto\,
  it proudly boasts its survival and longevity as a space within the lands
 cape of an ever-changing metropolis city. The interior of 918 Bathurst is
  a mix of modern design elements in conjunction with its preserved histor
 ic architecture\, notably its beautiful wooden ceilings. The show runs un
 til the end of October 2026\, don't miss it!
CATEGORIES:Art-Show/Gallery-Event,918-Bathurst-Arts-and-Culture-Center
