SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Fancy Cat Dance Performance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T160000
UID:6aaad4e36059b704112acb3f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Fancy Cat is a dance-theatre musical for children.  The perfo
 rmance follows a gender-expansive Grade 3 student navigating belonging\, s
 elf-expression\, and friendship.  Playful\, funny\, and heartfelt\, the w
 ork invites young audiences to explore what it means to be brave\, kind\, 
 and fully themselves.  After the performance\, children and families are 
 invited to Dance\, Sing\, and Play together in a joyful interactive worksh
 op.  Feel free to come in your Halloween costume too!  For children and 
 families.  All ages welcome.  Performance runs from 2-3pm followed by a
  workshop 3-4pm.  No registration required.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad4e36059b704112acb3f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
