BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae36e19ad40276591557544"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Storytelling -- works by Adira Rotstein
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261101T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T235959
UID:6ae36e19ad40276591557544@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of November\, the works of artist Adira R
 otstein are on display at\nDeer Park branch\n.\nAdira Rotstein is a Toront
 o artist\, writer and teacher. Her YA novels 'Little Jane Silver' and 'Lit
 tle Jane and the Nameless Isle' are published by Dundurn. She has experie
 nce in sequential art\, creating comic books and illustrating stories. She
  also loves experimenting with the boundaries of stopmotion and hand draw
 n animation. I am curious about the world in all beauty and absurdity\n"Us
 ually\, with my artwork I attempt to tell a story. People say I am able to
  imbue even inanimate objects with a personality\, human agency and warmth
 . People's faces\, their motions\, their discarded objects at rest tell s
 tories about where they have been\, what they have felt and where they are
  going. Slow down and see what they have to say. Even the smallest among 
 us has a perspective worth learning about and a beauty worth sensing."\nTh
 is exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Li
 brary provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations 
 across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural intere
 sts of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during 
 Deer Park's open hours. Please check the\nDeer Park branch\npage before yo
 ur visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit\nArtist: Adira Rotstein\nT
 itle of Piece: Little Jane Silver frontpiece\nMedium: water colour pencil
  on paper\nSize/Dimensions: small (up to 13 cm x 18 cm)
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae36e19ad40276591557544
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 School Age": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abfe43a9dbc2b002c8bcccd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_school_age
SUMMARY:Celebrate 60 years of Mimico Centennial Library
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261101T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T235959
UID:6abfe43a9dbc2b002c8bcccd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout November\, we're celebrating the\n60th anniversary
  of Mimico Centennial Library\n! Take a walk through history with our spec
 ial\nhistorical photo display\n\, featuring images and newspaper articles 
 of the library and surrounding Mimico community through the years. Discove
 r how our neighbourhood has changed and revisit the people\, places\, and 
 moments that have shaped our community.\n60 years of stories. 60 years of 
 memories. 60 years of community.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Front lawn and first floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abfe43a9dbc2b002c8bcccd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
