BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/electrical-engineering-ee-program-showcase/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Electrical Engineering (EE) Program Showcase
DTSTART:20261102T050000Z
DTEND:20261103T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T212900Z
UID:MEC-957c16082dfc126c427faaf49ea8c4c6@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261102T050000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Lassonde School of Engineering
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261023
DESCRIPTION:Electrical Engineering Program Showcase 2026\nDiscover | Explo
 re | Connect\nThe Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Scienc
 e (EECS) at York University’s Lassonde School of Engineering is pleased 
 to present the Electrical Engineering (EE) Program Showcase 2026\, an enga
 ging event designed to introduce students to the exciting opportunities\, 
 emerging technologies\, and real-world applications of electrical engineer
 ing.\nDate: Monday\, November 2\, 2026Time: 10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m.Locati
 on: BRG 125\, York University\nOrganized by Professor Ebrahim Ghafar-Zadeh
 \, Undergraduate Program Director in Engineering\, the showcase will featu
 re 10 faculty presentations\, live demonstrations\, laboratory tours\, and
  interactive discussions highlighting research and innovation across elect
 rical engineering.\nParticipants will explore a wide range of topics\, inc
 luding communications\, control systems\, optoelectronics\, analog and dig
 ital electronics\, artificial intelligence on chips\, power electronics\, 
 electric vehicles\, wearable and implantable devices\, and biomedical engi
 neering.\nThe event will provide a valuable opportunity for students\, par
 ticularly first-year engineering students\, to discover the breadth of ele
 ctrical engineering\, learn about research and career pathways\, interact 
 with faculty members and graduate students\, and experience cutting-edge t
 echnologies through demonstrations and laboratory visits.\nComplimentary l
 unch and networking opportunities will be provided\, allowing attendees to
  connect with faculty\, graduate students\, and peers in an informal and w
 elcoming environment.\nAll first-year engineering students are especially 
 encouraged to attend. Students from other years who are interested in elec
 trical engineering are also welcome.\nRegistration: Scan the QR code on th
 e event flyer to reserve your spot.\nJoin us to discover how electrical en
 gineering is shaping a smarter\, healthier\, and more sustainable future!\
 nBe Inspired. Discover Opportunities. Shape the Future.\n﻿\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023
LOCATION:125 Bergeron Centre for Engineering Excellence @ 11 Arboretum Ln\
 , North York\, ON M3J 2S5\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Ebrahim Ghafar-Zadeh":MAILTO:egz@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/electrical-engineering-ee-program-showc
 ase/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
