SUMMARY:Computer for Beginners 1 : Use a Mouse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T200000
UID:6add135ce06996003a85b325@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on how to use a mouse for absolute beginners with litt
 le or no computer experience.\nIn this first session you will:\nObserve an
 d practice how to operate a mouse effectively\nUnderstand various mouse po
 inters and cursors\nReview basic keyboard functions\nUse the mouse for bas
 ic Windows functions\nUpon completion of this class students will be able 
 to use a computer mouse at a basic level and will be able to go online for
  additional practice.\nPrerequisites: No computer experience required.\nFo
 rmat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nWhat Will You Learn?\nBasic tools such
  as the mouse and the keyboard\nHow to search online for information\, ser
 vices and entertainment\nHow to use email to keep in touch with family and
  friends\nInternet safety\, security and privacy\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\nAccessibility\nL
 ive or automated closed captioning\, sign language interpretation\, interv
 enor services\, or attendant services are available upon request. Please s
 ubmit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to:\ntpl.ca/accessibility-e
 vents\n.
LOCATION:Albion\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6add135ce06996003a85b325
