BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-week-5-financial-literacy/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Recovery College: YU & Balance Week 5 | Financial literacy: Unders
 tanding your student financial responsibility
DTSTART:20261103T170000Z
DTEND:20261103T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260901T142800Z
UID:MEC-bc8147ca69573b8a699c18e7ddbcfb48@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261103T170000Z
SEQUENCE:4
CATEGORIES:Bethune College,Calumet College,Colleges,Divisions and Special 
 Areas,Faculties,Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professio
 nal Studies,Financial Literacy Month,Glendon,Health Education &amp\; Promo
 tion,LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Community Hub,LA&amp\;PS Founders Coll
 ege,LA&amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp\;PS New College,LA&amp\;PS Vanier
  College,Lassonde School of Engineering,Learning Commons,Learning Skills S
 ervices,Stong College,Student Counselling, Health &amp\; Well-being,Studen
 ts,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260901
DESCRIPTION:Tuition\, textbooks\, bus fares\, lunch\, getting a coffee or 
 energy drink to get through your 2nd lecture of the day… expenses add up
  quickly when you’re in university.\nIn this week’s session of YU & Ba
 lance\, participants will:\n\nGet a realistic overview of their financial 
 responsibilities\nLearn how to save money on campus\, build balanced budge
 ts and understand the differences between types of student debt.\nStudents
  will also get a chance to ask Peer Health Educators for advice\, tips and
  strategize on how to be more money conscious.\n\nThis session is part of 
 a 6-week Recovery College series. For each session attended\, participants
  will receive $5 on their YU-card. To receive the gift card\, you must att
 end the full session (approximately 45–60 minutes). Unfortunately\, we
 ’re not able to provide gift cards for partial attendance. Gift cards wi
 ll be emailed after the session to the same email address used to register
  and join the session.\nSpace is limited\, and registration is offered on 
 a first-come\, first-served basis. If the session is full and you’d like
  to be added to the waitlist\, please email hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hsta
 cey@yorku.ca ). We’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. If you’re
  registered but can no longer attend\, please let us know as soon as you c
 an so we can offer your spot to another student.\nRegister for Financial L
