SUMMARY:LLM-enabled formal software verification
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T210000
UID:evt-mRGgHb6OFhNPPBw@events.lu.ma
DESCRIPTION:Address:\nCheck event page for more details.\n\nOn October 22\
 , Anthopic and Theorem published LLMs are making formal software verificat
 ion feasible at a much larger scale. This represents the first large-scale
  effort to use AI to apply formal verification to production software at t
 he assembly code level.\n\nGiles Edkins\, software engineer at Epoch AI\, 
 will talk about what this result mean\, and what it implies about software
  that we rely on today.\n\nDoors open at 6:00 PM and the talk starts at 6:
 45 PM. Come early to grab a seat and say hi! Because of building security\
 , someone from our team has to let each guest in\, and once the talk begin
 s…\n\nHosted by Jasmine Ren
LOCATION:https://luma.com/event/evt-mRGgHb6OFhNPPBw
URL:https://luma.com/trajec-gvn2
X-SOURCE:Luma Toronto Discover
END:VEVENT
