SUMMARY:Surviving Dementia Care:  The Realities of Family Caregiving
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T190000
UID:6adcd6bca85a2c003381d94e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us as author\, D. Grant Campbell discusses his recent boo
 k:  Surviving Dementia Care.  This program will address the experiences 
 of families who are caring for a loved one who is living with dementia\, i
 ncluding the various points of stress\, as well as the various points of j
 oy\, and ways in which caregivers learn to survive the experience.  Major
  topics include understanding the diagnosis\, communicating with the loved
  one\, choosing an assisted living facility\, and using music and the arts
  as a means of connection.
LOCATION:Elmbrook Park\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adcd6bca85a2c003381d94e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
