X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6913c3dd190003e7487d2"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Be Ready\, Toronto! Emergency Preparedness Workshop for Individual
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T140000
UID:6ab6913c3dd190003e7487d2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Emergencies can happen anywhere at any time. In Canada\, we fa
 ce numerous hazards\, including wildfires\, flooding\, heatwaves\, and ear
 thquakes. The Be Ready workshop aims to raise individual and household eme
 rgency preparedness. In this free workshop facilitated by the Toronto Emer
 gency Management Division of the City of Toronto\, in partnership with the
  Canadian Red Cross\, participants will learn about:\nThe potential hazard
 s and risks in their area\nHow to create an emergency plan\nHow to assembl
 e an emergency kit\nThe importance of social and support networks during e
 mergencies\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on th
 is form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librar
 ies Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be
  used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questi
 ons about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answ
 erline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, T
 oronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Downsview\, Lower Level Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6913c3dd190003e7487d2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac54b6f96ec3a003ad8b314"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Human Connection 101 Workshop Series for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T143000
UID:6ac54b6f96ec3a003ad8b314@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Human connection has a profound impact on our health and happi
 ness\, especially in our increasingly disconnected world. Join GenWell in 
 an interactive 4-week program series to learn practical ways to enhance so
 cial health\, understand the adverse effects of loneliness\, and discover 
 the benefits of building more meaningful connections. Receive a free socia
 l health workbook\, spend time with other participants after the workshops
 \, and enjoy some light refreshments provided.\nAbout GenWell: Founded in 
 2016\, GenWell is a registered charity whose mission is to make the world 
 a happier and healthier place by educating\, empowering\, and catalyzing f
 orty million Canadians about the importance of their social health.\nRegis
 tration required.\nThis is a four-week program. Participants are encourage
 d to attend every session.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey followin
 g the program. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 78
 9 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac54b6f96ec3a003ad8b314
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
