DESCRIPTION:This session is open to students from York’s Markham and Gle
 ndon campuses.\nBuilding connections can sometimes feel exciting\, awkward
  or even a little intimidating.\nIn this week’s session of YU & Balance\
 , we will focus on helping students feel more comfortable meeting new peop
 le\, strengthening the relationships they already have and recognizing wha
 t makes a connection healthy and supportive.\nStudents will explore ways t
 o:\n\nManage social anxiety\nBuild confidence in social settings\nThink in
 tentionally about who they can turn to for support.\n\nThis session is par
 t of a 6-week Recovery College series. For each session attended\, partici
 pants will receive $5 on their YU-card. To receive the gift card\, you mus
 t attend the full session (approximately 45–60 minutes). Unfortunately\,
  we’re not able to provide gift cards for partial attendance. Gift cards
  will be emailed after the session to the same email address used to regis
 ter and join the session.\nSpace is limited\, and registration is offered 
 on a first-come\, first-served basis. If the session is full and you’d l
 ike to be added to the waitlist\, please email hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:h
 stacey@yorku.ca ). We’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. If you
 ’re registered but can no longer attend\, please let us know as soon as 
 you can so we can offer your spot to another student.\nRegister for Making
  meaningful connections: Staying present in conversations ( https://yorku.
 zoom.us/meeting/register/L3DMNB_PTM2CK5eaWxjlhA#/registration )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261030
