X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b519baafa61002961b295"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Bring Your Problem: Can AI Help?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T200000
UID:6a9b519baafa61002961b295@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a recurring problem you think AI might help with? 
 A thing you keep doing by hand that feels like it should be easier? Bring 
 it. If you don't have one\, come help your neighbours with theirs.\nIn thi
 s interactive class with our Innovator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'
 ll learn a simple seven-step way to think about problems: what's annoying 
 you\, what you've tried\, what AI could actually do\, and where it would f
 ail. We'll gather real problems from the room\, sort them into groups\, an
 d map out what's worth solving with AI\, and what's better solved without 
 it. We'll also talk honestly about what an AI fix costs: your money\, your
  time\, and sometimes your private information. The problems AI could help
  with most are often the most personal\, and the most personal ones are wo
 rth the most care.\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 20
 26 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of
  the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be fill
 ed on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b519baafa61002961b295
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adf566b9dbc2b002c910e49"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:The Gravity Grand Prix
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T190000
UID:6adf566b9dbc2b002c910e49@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to design\, build\, and race! This high-speed engine
 ering challenge invites young adults (competing in teams of 2 ages 18-24) 
 to design the ultimate gravity-powered race car. Using professional 3D mod
 eling software and cutting-edge 3D printing technology\, your team will co
 mpete to see who can conquer the downhill track the fastest. The core of t
 his challenge is physics: maximizing kinetic energy while minimizing frict
 ion. How will you transform potential energy into pure speed?🛠️ The C
 hallenge Rules\nThe Software: All cars must be fully designed from scratch
  using OnShape. A brief Introduction to the software will be provided.\nTh
 e Material Limit: To keep the playing field level\, your final race car is
  strictly limited to a maximum of 30 grams of 3D printed filament and 2 to
 oth picks.\nFree Prototyping: Failure is part of engineering! Teams are en
 couraged to print\, test\, and redesign. Prototype prints are completely f
 ree throughout the design phase.\nThe Track: A straight\, downhill gravity
  track built for maximum acceleration.\n📅 Timeline & Important Dates\nD
 esign & Prototyping Week: Nov 4 to Nov 11— Access the DIH\, collaborate 
 with your partner\, and test your prototypes.\nRace Day: Nov 11 (Exactly o
 ne week after design week) — Family and friends are welcome to watch the
  final showdown!\n💡 Key Engineering Focus Areas to take home the trophy
 \, your team will need to think critically about:\nAerodynamics & Friction
 : How will you reduce air resistance and wheel friction to keep your car g
 liding?\nWeight Distribution: How can you strategically place your 30-gram
  limit to maximize downward momentum?
LOCATION:Malvern\, In the DIH
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adf566b9dbc2b002c910e49
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
