X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe6a9296ec3a003ad77b4f"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:The World Outside these Walls: Toronto's Asylum at 999 Queen Stree
 t West*
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T200000
UID:6abe6a9296ec3a003ad77b4f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Fifty years after its demolition\, the shadow of 999 Queen 
 Street West still looms large in Toronto. This presentation explores the a
 sylum's origins as a temporary facility within one of Toronto's first gaol
 s\, as well as the personalities and politics that brought such a mammoth 
 building to life. It will also look at its unique architecture\, its trea
 tment of patients and its presence as a Victorian tourist attraction.\nPre
 sented by Andrew Nablo\, historical interpreter at two Toronto History M
 useums: Colborne Lodge and For York.\nPreviously advertised as "The Shado
 w of 999 Queen Street West: Toronto's Lunatic Asylum"\nInformation Collect
 ion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
 )\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program reg
 istration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handl
 es your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl
 .ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe6a9296ec3a003ad77b4f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
