SUMMARY:*FULL -Human Connection 101 Workshop Series for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T150000
UID:6ad15d7ee06996003a83d3c8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Human connection has a profound impact on our health and happi
 ness\, especially in our increasingly disconnected world. Join GenWell in 
 an interactive 5-week (Oct 1\, 8\, 15\, 22\, 29 & Nov 5) program series to
  learn practical ways to enhance social health\, understand the adverse ef
 fects of loneliness\, and discover the benefits of building more meaningfu
 l connections. Receive a free social health workbook\, spend time with oth
 er participants after the workshops\, and enjoy some light refreshments pr
 ovided.\nAbout GenWell: Founded in 2016\, GenWell is a registered charity 
 whose mission is to make the world a happier and healthier place by educat
 ing\, empowering\, and catalyzing forty million Canadians about the import
 ance of their social health.\nRegistration full.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad15d7ee06996003a83d3c8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
