SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T153000
UID:6ad9201f29c3d60033318abf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The S. Walter Stewart Library and its neighbourhood is home to
  a variety of trees. Join the\nCity of Toronto Urban Forestry\nteam\nto ex
 plore the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recogn
 ize different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological im
 portance.\nFree program. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent
 /caregiver. Registration is required. Register online or call the branch a
 t 416-396-3975.\nThe tour will start and end in the front foyer of the S. 
 Walter Stewart Branch and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban For
 estry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route. Pleas
 e dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mitt
 ens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program takes pl
 ace rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, registrants 
 will be notified of an alternative date.\nPresented as part of TPL’s env
 ironmental program series\, Our Fragile Planet. TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\
 nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South C
 hapter.​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on th
 is form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librar
 ies Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be
  used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questi
 ons about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answ
 erline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, T
 oronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Front Foyer
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad9201f29c3d60033318abf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
