BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac832c4295b3b0033cb0300"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Club de lecture de North York Central Library
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:6ac832c4295b3b0033cb0300@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Aimez-vous lire en français? Avez-vous envie de participer à
  des discussions autour des livres dans une ambiance conviviale et déten
 due?\nRejoignez notre club de lecture en français! Venez échanger vos po
 ints de vue\, analyser ce qui vous a marqué avec le regard d'autres lecte
 urs\, et faire de belles découvertes littéraires.\nOn se réunit le 5 no
 vembre pour découvrir\n« La vie des gens libres » de Marie-Ève Lacasse
 \n. Le livre sera disponible en prêt à la Bibliothèque de North Central
 \nau 3ième étage\, au Département de langues\, littérature et beaux ar
 ts\, à partir du 9 octobre.\nSi vous voulez en savoir plus sur nos clubs 
 de lectures\, veuillez nous envoyer un courriel à\nprogrammesenfrancais@t
 pl.ca\nVeuillez noter que ce programme s’adresse aux personnes francopho
 nes ainsi qu’à celles ayant un niveau avancé en français. Il est néc
 essaire de pouvoir lire\, discuter et critiquer un livre avec une aisance 
 de communication en français.\nSi vous souhaitez pratiquer votre françai
 s mais que vous avez plutôt un niveau débutant ou intermédiaire\, nous 
 vous encourageons à découvrir nos cercles de conversation.\nLe sous-titr
 age en direct ou automatique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\, 
 les services d’intervenant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont dis
 ponibles sur demande. Veuillez soumettre votre demande au moins deux semai
 nes à l’avance à :\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac832c4295b3b0033cb0300
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696be0372c65973d001863f7"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Beaches Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:696be0372c65973d001863f7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion about the months book pick in 
 a welcoming\, relaxed setting. New members are always welcome and encourag
 ed to join.\nJanuary 8 - The Story of Us by Catherine Hernandez\nFebruary 
 5 - Death of the Author by Nnedi Okarofor\nMarch 5 - Wuthering Heights by 
 Emily Bronte\nApril 2 - The Siren's Call by Chris Hayes\nMay 7 - That Time
  I Loved You by Carianne Leung\nJune 4 - Any Other Way: How Toronto Got Qu
 eer by John Lorinc\nJuly 2 - The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy by Dougl
 as Adams\nAugust 6 - Demon Copperhead by Barbara Kingsolver\nSeptember 3 -
  Noopiming by Leanne Betasamosake Simpson\nOctober 1 - Shadow of the Wind 
 by Carlos Ruiz Zafon\nNovember 5 - House Divided by Alex Bozikovic\nDecemb
 er 3 - The Glass Hotel by Emily St. John Mandel\nCopies of our book club p
 icks will be set aside each month at the first-floor desk at Beaches Libra
 ry. These titles are also available as eBooks and eAudiobooks through Libb
 y\, and in alternate formats.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696be0372c65973d001863f7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac833b49dbc2b002c8d5e53"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Romance Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:6ac833b49dbc2b002c8d5e53@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the Romance Book Club\, where love stories take cen
 ter stage and every page promises a new adventure of the heart. Whether yo
 u're into slow burns\, second chances\, or enemies-to-lovers\, there's som
 ething here for every kind of romantic. Come read\, swoon\, and share your
  favorite moments with fellow book lovers.\nThe winning title for Brentwoo
 d's Romance Book Club on Thursday November 5 is\nHunt on Dark Waters\nby 
 Katee Robert.\nWe will save 5 minutes at the end of the meeting to discuss
  the the vote runner up\,\nThe Fake Mate\nby Lana Ferguson.\nLimited copie
 s will be available in branch for pick up from October 8.\nPlease note tha
 t this book club is for individuals 18+.\nDrop in\, no registration requir
 ed.\nHunt on Dark Waters\nThe Fake Mate
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac833b49dbc2b002c8d5e53
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc169be8cf1c005cafe983"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Creating your own Google Maps
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:6abc169be8cf1c005cafe983@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Your neighbourhood tells a story and the data to prove it alre
 ady exists. In this three-session series\, you will learn to find real civ
 ic data about your community\, plot it on an interactive map\, and turn wh
 at you discover into a powerful advocacy piece. No technical experience ne
 eded. Just curiosity about where you live and a desire to make it better.\
 nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minutes after the program for one-on-
 one consultations.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in Residence s
 eries focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28\, join pr
 ograms\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology strategi
 st Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create positive cha
 nge in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc169be8cf1c005cafe983
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
