X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a88ef9ed2e00384f513d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Ujima Network
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T130000
UID:6aa1a88ef9ed2e00384f513d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A free group program that explores mental wellness through a c
 ulturally responsive lens grounded in the Black Model of Health and Wellbe
 ing and the principles of Nguzo Saba. Participants build self-awareness\, 
 learn about the impacts of social determinants of health\, and support one
  another through talk circles and group activities.\nFree registration is 
 required\, speak to library staff for assistance.\nThis program is in coll
 aboration with\nTAIBU Community Health Centre\n.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a88ef9ed2e00384f513d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adfa22d0b801373af911759"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Cyanotype Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T113000
UID:6adfa22d0b801373af911759@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What materials and processes existed before Adobe Photoshop? J
 oin us for a hands-on analog image making workshop to create a Cyanotype. 
 The Cyanotype is a photographic printing technique sensitive to a limited 
 near ultraviolet and blue light spectrum. It involves layering objects and
  transparencies. All are welcome!\nWe will supply all materials\, but feel
  free to bring an object or 2D silhouette for a contact print.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Activity Room (first floor)
