UID:TKF/6755f42da02aaf1c2599e7ae/24617/29900100/0/0
DTSTART:20261106T230000Z
DTEND:20261107T003000Z
URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/24617/1794006000000
SUMMARY: Imaginary Expedition
DESCRIPTION:Imaginary Expedition is a Toronto-based duo of Victoria Dobbs
  and Glyph Greenleaf who combine folk songwriting with early music compos
 ition techniques and intimate\, unamplified performance practice. The ens
 emble draws people closer\, quietly pushing the limits of what can be ach
 ieved with only their alto and baritone voices and a classical guitar. Th
 eir songs alternate between the lead vocalists\, and gravitate toward due
 ts with equal importance on both vocal lines.\n\n\nThe name Imaginary Exp
 edition reflects the experience the duo creates. Their songs spark daydre
 ams and send listeners on journeys through memory\, grief\, gratitude\, a
 nd self-reflection. Their lyrics journey through emotional terrain shaped
  by the vivid changing seasons of the North\, with imagery drawn from gre
 at lakes\, old-growth forests\, open prairies\, wetlands\, shield rock\, 
 and luminous skies.\n\n\nVictoria and Glyph began writing together in Aug
 ust 2024 and performing together regularly in September 2025\, after year
 s of separate professional music careers. The duo has developed their liv
 e show and generated momentum through intimate listening rooms\, festival
  stages\, house concerts\, and industry showcases. The duo has appeared a
 t JP Music Festival in Boston (2025)\, and Toronto’s Winterfolk Blues + R
 oots Festival and Toronto Folk Festival (2026).\n\n\nTheir debut singles 
 “Winter Lullaby” and “The Ones Who Are Gone” capture the acoustic realism
  of sitting in a room with the performers\, whose voices move in harmony 
 and counterpoint with Glyph’s lap-style classical guitar. The songs\, whi
 ch explore how we carry the memories of those we have lost\, have receive
 d airplay on folk and indie radio in Canada\, the USA\, and Australia. Wi
 th the support of a FACTOR Artist Development grant the duo has begun pro
 duction of a full-length album in the same live-off-the-floor format.\n\n
 \nDoors: 6pm\n\nConcert: 6:30-7:30pm\n\nAll ages welcome.\n\n$10-$12 adva
 nce / $15 at the door\n\nTickets: www.showpass.com/imaginary-expedition-a
 t-burdock-music-hall/ https://www.showpass.com/imaginary-expedition-at-bu
 rdock-music-hall/
CATEGORIES:Concert,Burdock-Music-Hall
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/6755f3e6a02aaf
 1c2599e757/6adee31e3d5e247eea8d31d0/scaled_1024.jpg
