UID:6a4809214407827f8aa92cda@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Humber Summit Library and its neighbourhood is home to a v
 ariety of trees. Join the\nCity of Toronto Urban Forestry\nteam\nto explor
 e the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize 
 different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological import
 ance.\nFree program. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/car
 egiver. Registration is required.\nPresented as part of TPL’s environmen
 tal program series\, Our Fragile Planet. The series is generously supporte
 d by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.\nThe tour\nwill be
  guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\,
  unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly fo
 r this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, c
 omfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the event of
  severe inclement weather\, registrants will be notified of an alternative
  date.
LOCATION:Humber Summit
