  Program in Social Work,Graduate Program in Socio-Legal Studies,Graduate P
 rogram in Sociology,Graduate Program in Theatre,Graduate Program in Theatr
 e, Dance &amp\; Performance Studies,Graduate Program in Translation Studie
 s,Graduate Program in Visual Art,Health Education &amp\; Promotion,LA&amp\
 ;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Founders College,LA&amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&
 amp\;PS New College,LA&amp\;PS Vanier College,Osgoode Professional Develop
 ment,School of Continuing Studies,Schulich School of Business,Student Coun
 selling, Health &amp\; Well-being,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature 
 and Part-time Students
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261005
DESCRIPTION:Are you a graduate or mature student interested in shaping men
 tal health and well‑being programming that reflects your lived experienc
 e at York University? This co‑design opportunity is for you.\nIn collabo
 ration with Ontario Shores Centre for Mental Health Sciences\, Student Cou
 nselling\, Health & Well‑being (SCHW) is expanding our recovery college 
 programming— a series of health and well‑being workshops designed to h
 elp students thrive amid the unique pressures of advanced study\, research
 \, caregiving\, work and life transitions.\nWhat will we do?\nYou and a sm
 all group of fellow graduate and mature students will work alongside SCHW 
 and Ontario Shores to co‑create the next set of recovery college worksho
 ps launching in Winter/Spring 2027. Together\, you will shape workshop top
 ics\, content and learning activities and how sessions are delivered and f
 acilitated.\nWhat will we learn?\n\nRecovery college principles and how ed
 ucation rooted in lived experience supports mental health\nCo‑design met
 hods for building impactful student‑centered programming\nHow to draw on
  your own experiences navigating academic and life‑stage pressures as a 
 source of expertise\nHow to collaborate as part of a design team to create
  accessible\, empowering mental health workshops\n\nProgram Details\nThis 
 5‑week co‑design series runs virtually on Mondays from 1:15 to 2:15 PM
 \, from November 9 to December 7. Participation is open to all graduate an
 d mature students.\nHonorarium\nIn appreciation for your support\, partici
 pants will receive $25 loaded directly to their YU card for each session a
 ttended in full (up to $125 for completing all five sessions).\nNote: Co
 ‑Design sessions run for one hour. To receive the honorarium for a sessi
 on\, you must attend the full session. If you are unable to attend the ful
 l hour or experience technical difficulties\, please contact Holly Stacey 
 directly at hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hstacey@yorku.ca ).\nRegistration\nS
 pace is limited (maximum 12 participants) and offered on a first‑come\, 
 first‑served basis. Registration is open to mature undergraduate student
 s\, graduate students and School of Continuing Studies students. If spots 
 are full but you would like to be added to a waiting list in the event of 
 cancellations\, please contact Holly Stacey at hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:h
 stacey@yorku.ca ). Selected participants will receive additional details a
 nd Zoom instructions.\nRegister for Recovery College Co-Design Course for 
 Graduate & Mature Students ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/t4xHUE
 9yRX6TSiSjoGpg3g )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261005
LOCATION:Online (Zoom)
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-co-design-course-for-g
 raduate-mature-students/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
