SUMMARY:Building Interview Skills for Younger Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T180000
UID:6ab410264ea230006f351e7e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​It is very likely that someone will encounter their first i
 nterview experience in their youth\, yet the skills required to complete a
  successful interview are often unpracticed and unknown to them. This prog
 ram will introduce skills such as speaking professionally\, what kind of q
 uestions to expect\, interview processes\, preparation and learning to exu
 de genuine confidence.  Increase your potential for success by learning th
 ese integral skills to acing an interview!  Presented by Victoria Tung.\
 nInformation Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery\, and evaluation. Questions about 
 how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline sta
 ff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Deer Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab410264ea230006f351e7e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
