SUMMARY:Wednesday Night Movie: 1945 (2017)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T200000
UID:6adccfbfa85a2c003381d836@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a viewing of our Wednesday Night Movie\n: 1945\n(2
 017)\nDirected by\n: Ferenc Torok\nStarring\n: Peter Rudolf\, Bence Tasnad
 i\, Tamas Szabo Kimmel\n1 hrs 31 minutes\nRated G\n12 August 1945\, 11 AM.
  Two mysterious strangers dressed in black appear at the railway station o
 f a Hungarian village. In the shadow of Russian occupation\, the people of
  the village are preparing for the wedding of the son of the clerk\, but t
 he bride's former fiancé returns from captivity. Within a few hours\, eve
 rything changes. Secrets\, sins\, reckoning\, love\, betrayal\, confrontat
 ion. This is a film dealing with the aftermath of war.\nLanguage: Hungaria
 n | Subtitles in English                    Filmed in Black & White
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Auditorium
