CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:This session is open to students from York’s Markham and Gle
 ndon campuses.\nHave you ever googled yourself? Or maybe an old friend fro
 m high school? Once something is shared online\, it becomes easily findabl
 e with just one search.\nIn this week’s session of YU & Balance\, partic
 ipants will:\n\nGet a better grasp on what digital footprint is\nHow to fi
 nd reliable sources of information\nUnderstand algorithms\, social media f
 eeds and strategize on how to mindfully engage AI\n\nThis session is part 
 of a 6-week Recovery College series. For each session attended\, participa
 nts will receive $5 on their YU-card. To receive the gift card\, you must 
 attend the full session (approximately 45–60 minutes). Unfortunately\, w
 e’re not able to provide gift cards for partial attendance. Gift cards w
 ill be emailed after the session to the same email address used to registe
 r and join the session.\nSpace is limited\, and registration is offered on
  a first-come\, first-served basis. If the session is full and you’d lik
 e to be added to the waitlist\, please email hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hst
 acey@yorku.ca ). We’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. If you’r
 e registered but can no longer attend\, please let us know as soon as you 
 can so we can offer your spot to another student.\nRegister for Algorithms
  & AI literacy: Supporting your digital footprint ( https://forms.students
 .yorku.ca/view.php?id=500072 )\n
