X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:THE SPECTACLE OF VIOLENCE AS A SPECTRE
DTSTART:20261112T173000Z
DTEND:20261112T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T040200Z
UID:MEC-dc9dab195b7aeefb54a4f8bfa798d2da@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261112T173000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Glendon Political Science
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261029
DESCRIPTION:Should violence be a source of entertainment? How does this co
 mmercialization blur the line between political violence and popular cultu
 re?\nWith Dr. Marie-Hélène Larochelle as our guide—Glendon’s Departm
 ent of Global Communication and Cultures Chair—join us as we examine the
  contemporary fascination with violence\, its normalization in our contemp
 orary storytelling\, and the implications of its commercialization in toda
 y’s culture. Light snacks and refreshments will be provided!\nEveryone i
 s welcome!\nRSVP here: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdhSoYYiua
 RnaiPT_d4_6brqZaST0rAqrAy8_ORrFZws52GHw/viewform ( https://docs.google.com
 /forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdhSoYYiuaRnaiPT_d4_6brqZaST0rAqrAy8_ORrFZws52GHw/viewfo
 rm )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029
