SUMMARY:Senior Social: Make A Will with the Ontario Bar Association
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T150000
UID:6adcd74f901b02002cc4d855@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Make a Will Month and TPL is delighted to host the
  Ontario Bar Association. Learn about the importance of having a will and 
 powers of attorney for you and your family. A member of the Ontario Bar As
 sociation who practices Trusts and Estates Law will speak about the elemen
 ts of a will\, what happens if you don’t have one\, what are powers of a
 ttorney\, why they are important and special considerations to keep in min
 d when preparing your estate and care plans. Note\, this program is for ge
 neral information only\, not for drafting individual wills.
LOCATION:St. Clair/Silverthorn\, Community Room 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adcd74f901b02002cc4d855
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
