SUMMARY: Toronto Aces & Aros' Showcase & Zine Launch
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Aces & Aros is hosting a Showcase performance to cele
 brate the recent Ace Awareness Week and the launch of Issue # 3 of the To
 ronto Aces & Aros Zine!\n\n  * Sunday\, November 15th (4-6pm) -- performa
 nces start sharply at 4:30pm\n  * 32 Lisgar (GladDay)\, 2nd floor (elevat
 or near door)\n  * Event is free to attend\n\nCome and watch the Showcase
  of asexual/ace & aromantic/aro spectrum community performers! (Most perf
 ormers also bring experience as trans & non-binary\, neurodivergent and d
 isabled community members.)\nAnd pick up a brand new copy of the 3rd issu
 e of Toronto Aces & Aros’ zine!\nAudience members welcome of all identiti
 es!\n\nYou can also pre-order your copy of Toronto Aces & Aro’s Zine # 3 
 “Access” (or back-issues) forms.gle/b168AEnXToWB7hSg8 https://forms.gle/b
 168AEnXToWB7hSg8\n\n*** Accessibility ***\n\n  * Wheelchair accessible (f
 lat entrance\, elevator inside)\n  * Armless chairs\n  * Accessible\, all
 -gender washrooms\n  * ASL interpretation (See Note)*\n  * Masks required
  (provided if needed) except if communicating by ASL\n  * We are also hop
 ing to project the text of performances on-screen but this is still in pr
 ogress\n\n* Note: Performance-based ASL interpretation is extremely chall
 enging and takes many hours of preparation. Normally an event like this r
 equires 2 ASL interpreters with extensive performance-based experience.\n
 \n  * Due to limited resources (as an un-funded grassroots community grou
 p)\, we are only able to secure 1 ASL interpreter with extensive performa
 nce-based experience and 1 ASL interpreter newer to performance-based int
 erpretation (both are generously working at discounted rate).\n  * Unfort
 unately\, this means the interpretation of the performance portion may no
 t be as effective as it should be\, despite the interpreters’ best effort
 s. We regret these limitations.\n  * Both interpreters are experienced wo
 rking with (and are members of) local 2SLGBTQ+ communities.
CATEGORIES:Spoken-Word/Poetry,Concert,Dance---Performance---Theatre,Book-
 Launch,Glad-Day-Lit
