SUMMARY:Garden with Purpose: Practical Ecological Gardening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T190000
UID:6ac3bad29d27a000454eac67@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Doors open at 5:30pm to mingle and chat with fellow nature and
  environmental enthusiasts! Program starts at 6pm.\nYou have the power to
  create real ecological change — right in your own backyard. In this int
 roductory program\, discover the core principles of ecological gardening a
 nd learn how to transform your garden into a space that’s both environme
 ntally responsible and visually stunning. A Toronto Master Gardener will p
 rovide guidance on how to create habitat\, manage water wisely\, and reduc
 e your ecological impact — all while cultivating a landscape rich with b
 eauty and year-round interest. Suitable for gardeners of any skill level\,
  with any kind of outdoor space.\nRegistration required.\nThis program is 
 part of TPL's Our Fragile Planet program series\, supported by Friends of 
 Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac3bad29d27a000454eac67
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
