SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 10/laptop-students-sources_James-Robertson-6-1.jpg
CATEGORIES:LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Community Hub,LA&amp\;PS Founder
 s College,LA&amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp\;PS New College,LA&amp\;PS 
 Student Success,LA&amp\;PS Students All,LA&amp\;PS Students-Graduate,LA&am
 p\;PS Students-International,LA&amp\;PS Students-Undergrad,LA&amp\;PS Vani
 er College,LA&amp\;PS Writing Centre,LA&amp\;PS Writing Department
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261002
DESCRIPTION:Discover strategies for integrating sources into your writing 
 so that your own ideas respond to those of other scholars. Learn when\, ho
 w\, and why crediting your sources is so important in university writing.\
 nThe Write Now! series consists of four workshops\, each of which focuses 
 on one aspect of the writing process:\nWorkshop 1: Analyze Your Assignment
 \nWorkshop 2: Construct an Argument\nWorkshop 3: Meaningful Citations\nWor
 kshop 4: Effective Editing\nAt the end of each workshop\, you’ll receive
  access to a quiz\, which you will need to complete within 72 hours of the
  workshop date. If you pass the quiz\, you will receive a badge\, which wi
 ll be recorded on the Write Now! eClass site.\nIf you attend all four work
 shops and pass each workshop’s quiz within one academic calendar year\, 
 you’ll attain a Certificate of Completion that can be added to your resu
 me and professional networking sites\, such as LinkedIn. Students must joi
 n workshop in the first 15 minutes and attend at least 60 minutes of it to
  take the test.\nClick to authenticate and join!\nClick Here\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002
LOCATION:Online Zoom
ORGANIZER;CN="James Robertson":MAILTO:jroberts@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/meaningful-citations-6/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
