BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc216511bbf300684a75fc"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Storytelling Using Data & AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T200000
UID:6abc216511bbf300684a75fc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Every community has problems. This series gives you the tools 
 to do something about them. Over three sessions you will define a real civ
 ic challenge in your neighbourhood\, design a creative response\, and buil
 d something: a digital campaign\, a poster\, a video pitch\, or even a 3D-
 printed prototype that communicates your idea to the public. Come ready to
  think\, build\, and be heard.\nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minute
 s after the program for one-on-one consultations.\nThis program is part of
  TPL's Innovator in Residence series focused on civic innovation. From Oct
 ober 5 to November 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultat
 ions led by technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology c
 an help you create positive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.c
 a/iir\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Question
 s about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answer
 line staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Tor
 onto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc216511bbf300684a75fc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"YOHOMO": "https://www.yohomo.ca/event/when-the-dead-are-kept-from-us"}
X-SOURCE-ID:yohomo
SUMMARY:When The Dead Are Kept From Us
DTSTART:20261117T190000
DTEND:20261117T190000
UID:27284a8bd2aa889de13f93e844fb460a@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer Death Salon is a virtual community space for all 2SLGBTQ
 IA+ people to come together to discuss death\, dying and grief. How do we 
 honor our dead when they are kept from us? What happens to us when we are 
 denied our chance to mourn? Let&#x27\;s come together to learn about and p
 ractice building ritual for grief when we are othered. Colleen (ʻoia/they
 /them) of Death Doula Does will guide participants through practical skill
 s for honoring our mourning and grief in rituals when we have no body to h
 old. Colleen is a Kanaka Maoli\, Queer\, mutual aider\, community-oriented
  death doula. Supporting those dying\, caregivers for the dying\, and grie
 vers for over a decade\, their work focuses on art-based grief spaces\, qu
 eer end-of-life planning\, and teaching how to be with death. (FOR MORE IN
 FO SEE TICKET LINK PROVIDED)
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/when-the-dead-are-kept-from-us
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
