BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Bicycling Network": "https://www.tbn.ca/widget/event-6890066"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_bicycling_network
SUMMARY:City Walk - Arts and Ghosts (St Clair to Mount Pleasant)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T130000
UID:199dbfd692cd1535badc562511d7aac0@tbn.ca
DESCRIPTION:Meet at about 10:00 AM on Pleasant Blvd outside the south entr
 ance of St Clair Station (on the Yonge Line)\, just west of Yonge St and o
 ne street south of St Clair. We will begin the walk at 10:10 sharp. Jennie
  will be leading this walk. We will go for a total of about 7.7 Km in two 
 loops. First about 3.5 Km into Mount Pleasant Cemetery and back to the sta
 rt\, then about 4 Km over to Avenue Road and back\, looking at some works 
 of art along the way. Most of the walk will be on city streets or paved pa
 ths\, with a brief excursion onto grass. We will also look at some outdoor
  artwork in the area. No scheduled subway outages have been posted yet\, b
 ut please check https://www.ttc.ca/service-advisori...
URL:https://www.tbn.ca/widget/event-6890066
X-SOURCE:Toronto Bicycling Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/sleep-qigong-self-acupressure/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T113000
DTSTAMP:20261031T012759
CREATED:20260911T194406Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001T180138Z
UID:10002033-1795082400-1795087800@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Sleep Qigong & Self-Acupressure
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an introduction to Sleep Qigong & Self-Acupressure!\nSleep issues can occur at different times during our lives in a variety of ways and for different reasons. You might have trouble falling asleep; perhaps you can fall asleep easily but wake up several times throughout the night; you might fall asleep but wake up too early feeling you haven’t slept quite enough; or you suffer from insomnia. Stress\, anxiety\, depression\, age\, worry\, and other factors can all contribute to sleep complications.\n \nIn this session\, I will demonstrate and guide you through some holistic and non-invasive ways to deal with sleep issues. They will include simple self-acupressure\, gentle qigong\, helpful tips\, and calming breathing exercises.\n \nWhether you experience occasional or chronic sleep problems\, this session can provide you with some alternative ways to deal with it.\nThursday\, November 19\, 10 to 11:30 a.m.\nRegistration: Public $25\, TBG Member $20 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout David Leopold\nSifu David Leopold has been practicing\, studying\, researching and teaching martial and healing arts since 1994.\n \nIn 1999\, Sifu David achieved his black belt in Shaolin Kung Fu. Since 1999\, Sifu David has received numerous certifications in Tachi and weapon forms\, and seven Qigong routines. In 2009\, Sifu David received his Usui Reiki master certification from the Naturopathic School of Medicine in Toronto.\n \nIn 2012\, Sifu David travelled to China to compete in the International Wushi Competition in Shanghai. He brought home 2 gold and a bronze medal.\n \nBy combining all these modalities and experiences\, Sifu David brings a unique style of teaching that includes technique\, philosophy\, and practicality. Sify David’s approach to teaching is relaxed and he believes Taichi and Qigong practice should be useful in everyday life and enjoyable to do.\n \nSifu David has a passion for martial and healing arts. His holistic approach to wellness includes physical\, emotional\, spiritual and nutritional well-being. Sifu David continues to improve his skills as a practitioner\, teacher/ mentor\, and hopes to teach for the rest of his life.\n \nSifu David’s words of wisdom:\n \n“To be a master of what you do\, you must first be a master unto yourself.”\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/sleep-qigong-self-acupressure/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Avenue East\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Education,Wellness
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/868bb9a88cfd1e6c17f57ee1daead311.jpg
END:VEVENT
