DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies (FGS)\, the Centre for Researc
 h on Latin America and the Caribbean (CERLAC)\, and the Harriet Tubman Ins
 titute are pleased to invite you to the reintroduction of a dedicated comm
 unity space for Black graduate students at York University.\nWhen: Thursda
 y\, November 19\, 2026\nTime: 12:00 p.m.\nWhere: York Lanes 321\, Keele Ca
 mpus\nThis space is designed to foster connection\, community and academic
  support\, providing a place where Black graduate scholars can come togeth
 er\, build relationships\, share experiences\, support one another and fin
 d a sense of belonging across disciplines and programs.\nJoin us as we cel
 ebrate this important milestone and gather with students\, faculty and sch
 olars from across the York community. The open house will feature engaging
  conversations\, meaningful storytelling\, games\, and opportunities to co
 nnect and build new networks.\nSpace is limited and registration is requir
 ed. Please register to attend the open house. RSVP Form ( https://fgs.apps
 01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=355204 )\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261022
