SUMMARY:Cercle de conversation : Parlons cinéma ! French Conversation Cir
 cle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T193000
UID:6ad12cf5901b02002cc2b7a7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:[English version follows]\nPratiquez votre français en explor
 ant le monde du cinéma francophone.\nRegardez le film chez vous\n\, ensui
 te assistez à la rencontre pour discuter du film. Tous les niveaux sont b
 ienvenus. Les places sont limitées donc vous devez vous inscrire.\nPour l
 e mois de novembre\, nous allons discuter du film\nIl pleuvait des oiseaux
 \n(\nAnd the Birds Rained Down\n) (Canada\, 2019) . Le film est disponib
 le sur la plateforme\nKanopy\n. Le film est en français avec sous-titres
  en anglais.\nPractice your French and explore the world of French-languag
 e cinema. Every month we meet to discuss a French-language film that you\n
 watch at home\nbefore the meeting. All levels are welcome. Please register
  as places are limited.\nIn November\, we will discuss the film\nAnd the B
 irds Rained Down\n(Canada\, 2019). The film is available to stream for fr
 ee with your TPL library card on\nKanopy\n. The film is presented in Frenc
 h with English subtitles.\nInformation Collection Notice\n: The personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under 
 the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inform
 ation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and 
 evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789
  Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\nACCESSIBILITÉ\nLe sous-titrage en di
 rect ou automatique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les servi
 ces d’intervenant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles 
 sur demande. Veuillez soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l
 ’avance à :\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Discussion Room\, 3rd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad12cf5901b02002cc2b7a7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6962837f91e4576f847bd105"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Between the Lines Bookclub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T200000
UID:6962837f91e4576f847bd105@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Due to renovations the Bookclub will take place in Scadding Co
 urt Community Center in Room 4 (same building)\, participants will be resp
 onsible in sourcing copies of the monthly titles themselves as the branch
  will not be open to the public during this time. We apologize for the inc
 onvenience!\nBecome a page-turner by joining the Between the Lines Book Cl
 ub! Here\, we embark on a new chapter with every read\, diving into a worl
 d of endless possibilities. From gripping thrillers to heartwarming coming
 -of-age tales\, or a sprinkle of fantasy adventures\, there's something fo
 r everyone. Whether you're a die-hard fan of one genre or love mixing thin
 gs up\, you'll find a place here to discuss\, share\, and connect with fel
 low readers. Ready to explore different worlds and discover your next favo
 rite book? Join us and let's turn the page together!\nFriday November 16: 
 A Gentleman in Moscow by Amor Towles\nSet in Moscow in 1922\,\nA Gentlem
 an in Moscow\nby Amor Towles follows Count Alexander Rostov\, a refined Ru
 ssian aristocrat sentenced by a Bolshevik tribunal to house arrest in the 
 grand Metropol Hotel\, where he must spend the rest of his life confined w
 ithin its walls. As the world outside undergoes dramatic political and soc
 ial change\, the Count gradually transforms his restricted circumstances i
 nto a life rich with unexpected friendships\, meaningful encounters\, and 
 quiet adventures. From navigating the hotel's intricate social world to fo
 rming a particularly meaningful bond with a young girl named Nina\, Rostov
  discovers new perspectives on love\, loyalty\, personal growth\, and the 
 passage of time. Elegant\, witty\, and deeply moving\, the novel explores 
 the nature of freedom\, the importance of human connection\, and the possi
 bility of finding purpose and beauty even when life takes an unexpected tu
 rn.
LOCATION:Sanderson - Closed\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6962837f91e4576f847bd105
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
