UID:6ae13fede06996003a86619b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come and up your photography game! Explore how to handle and s
 hoot DSLR and mirrorless cameras while learning the basics of how to take 
 a great photo.\nWhether you just want to take better pictures on your smar
 tphone or graduate to a professional DSLR or mirrorless camera\, join us f
 or a class on the basics of digital photography. We will go over the basic
  settings that go into producing a good photo and talk about camera settin
 gs\, lenses\, and lighting.\nRegistration opens 2 weeks prior to class.\nC
 amera equipment will be provided for this class.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Flemingdon Park\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae13fede06996003a86619b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
