BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-6-managing-academic-stress-and-exam-anxiety/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Recovery College: YU & Balance Week 6 | Managing academic stress a
 nd exam anxiety
DTSTART:20261126T170000Z
DTEND:20261126T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260918T190900Z
UID:MEC-44646f4cd5c4c7d9c6c3f2f6be4dcb1f@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261126T170000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Academic Advising &amp\; Student Success,Glendon,Markham Campus
 ,Markham Student Accessibility Services,Student Leaders at Markham (SLAM),
 Student Life
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:This session is open to students from York’s Markham and Gle
 ndon campuses.\nSometimes\, a single grade can get inside your head and ma
 ke you question your ability to succeed in your program. The pressure to 
 earn high marks\, often called “academic perfectionism”\, is something
  many post-secondary students experience.\nIn this week’s session of YU 
 & Balance\, participants will explore how stress affects academic performa
 nce and learn practical strategies to manage it as you prepare for exam se
 ason. By the end of the session\, participants will have tools to recogni
 ze stress\, respond to it effectively\, and protect your confidence during
  exams.\nThis session is part of a 6-week Recovery College series. For eac
 h session attended\, participants will receive $5 on their YU-card. To rec
 eive the gift card\, you must attend the full session (approximately 45–
 60 minutes). Unfortunately\, we’re not able to provide gift cards for pa
 rtial attendance. Gift cards will be emailed after the session to the same
  email address used to register and join the session.\nSpace is limited\, 
 and registration is offered on a first-come\, first-served basis. If the s
 ession is full and you’d like to be added to the waitlist\, please email
  hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hstacey@yorku.ca ). We’ll reach out if a spot
  becomes available. If you’re registered but can no longer attend\, plea
 se let us know as soon as you can so we can offer your spot to another stu
 dent.\nRegister for Managing academic stress and exam anxiety ( https://fo
 rms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=501019 )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261027
LOCATION:Virtual Event
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-6-mana
 ging-academic-stress-and-exam-anxiety/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-balance-build-week-6-managing-academic-stress-exam-anxiety/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Recovery College- Balance & Build Week 6: Managing Academic Stress
  & Exam Anxiety
DTSTART:20261126T170000Z
DTEND:20261126T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260826T162800Z
UID:MEC-dcfca14d2ff6809ddb09db45c2c68693@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261126T170000Z
SEQUENCE:5
CATEGORIES:Health Education &amp\; Promotion,Markham Campus
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260826
DESCRIPTION:All it takes is one below average or even just average mark to
  get inside your head and begin doubting yourself and your ability to succ
 eed in your program. The pressure to get high marks\, or academic perfecti
 onism\, is commonly experienced by students in university. This week\, stu
 dents will explore the effects of stress on academic performance\, learn s
 trategies for managing and coping with stress to tackle exam season. \n \
 nRegister & learn more at https://students.yorku.ca/counselling/health-edu
 cation/recovery-college\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260826
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-balance-build-week-6-m
 anaging-academic-stress-exam-anxiety/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
