SUMMARY:AI for Small Business and Entrepreneurs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T200000
UID:6a9b51b8aafa61002961b2a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You've got the business idea. Now come the thousand questions:
  who's my customer\, what's the market\, how do I pitch this?\nIn this cla
 ss led by our Innovator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'll use AI as a 
 research and planning partner for small business. We'll practice together 
 on a sample business\, turning rough ideas into business plans\, digging i
 nto markets\, drafting customer-discovery questions\, and building useful 
 low-maintenance automation. The most valuable thing you'll get is usually 
 a better question to be tested in the real world. Whether you're starting 
 or growing\, you'll leave with an experiment you can run on your own busin
 ess this week.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. 
 Computers are provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is r
 equired and will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will
  not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter thi
 s time\, remaining seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basi
 s until capacity is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hand
 s-on program\, please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used i
 n This Program\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools
  (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own ac
 count for this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Residen
 t’s guidance throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using
  AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior
  to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nRevie
 w privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy
  policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy po
 licy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\n
 Information Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about ho
 w the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff
  at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4
 W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51b8aafa61002961b2a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a748e6bf4e5db3d00c6d3fd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Knit\, Crochet & Crafting Circle - evening sessions\, featuring a 
 therapy cat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T193000
UID:6a748e6bf4e5db3d00c6d3fd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bring your own knit\, crochet\, or other portable craft proje
 ct\, and hang out and chat with other crafters while you work! Once a mo
 nth\, we will gather in the evening for cozy crafts to unwind after a long
  day.\nThis session will feature special guest Ziggy the cat and friends 
 from One Health Partners.\nZiggy the therapy cat\nRegistration is required
  if you wish to take part in small-group interactions with the therapy cat
 \, as space is limited. Drop ins may be accommodated\, pending space avail
 ability.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Question
 s about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answer
 line staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Tor
 onto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd floor: \nRoom 1 (Sep 28\, Nov 30
 \, Dec 28)\; Room 2/3 (Oct 26)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a748e6bf4e5db3d00c6d3fd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
