SUMMARY:E-Bikes in Toronto: A Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T200000
UID:6ada58c8377296003a4dd2de@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about e-bikes in Toronto?\nJoin us for an open discuss
 ion to learn more about e-bikes in Toronto.\nGuest speakers\nAlbert Koehl 
 and Beth Savan\nwill explore the benefits of e-bikes and address common co
 ncerns and complaints about their use in the city. Topics will include the
  need for regulatory reform\, options for managing e-bike use\, concerns a
 bout the potential danger of e-bike batteries\, and more.\nAn introduction
  to the topic will be followed by a Question and Answer period.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada58c8377296003a4dd2de
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
