X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aca8a4f035faf0033dbbecd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Runnymede Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T193000
UID:6aca8a4f035faf0033dbbecd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion of Claire Keegan's\,\nSmall Th
 ings Like These\nIt is 1985\, in an Irish town. During the weeks leading u
 p to Christmas\, Bill Furlong\, a coal and timber merchant\, faces his bus
 iest season. As he does the rounds\, he feels the past rising up to meet h
 im - and encounters the complicit silences of a small community controlled
  by the Church.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aca8a4f035faf0033dbbecd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad11ef5a76c9f3e2ae849ac"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Tuesday Night Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T194500
UID:6ad11ef5a76c9f3e2ae849ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us on Tuesday December the first\, at 6:30 p.m. t
 o talk about the novel\nNews of the world\n. In post–Civil War Texas\, a
  traveling news reader must escort a young girl raised by Indigenous peopl
 e across a dangerous frontier to a family she barely remembers. Their peri
 lous journey becomes an unforgettable adventure of survival\, unlikely fri
 endship\, and the search for belonging. Get a copy at the first-floor circ
 ulation desk while supplies last. If you prefer an eBook or eAudiobook\, a
 sk library staff how to access them.\nFor more information\, please call M
 aria A. Shchuka Library at 416-394-1000.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad11ef5a76c9f3e2ae849ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad774ab7a8e0037c241ff"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Intercultural Communication Competency is a Superpower
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T200000
UID:6aaad774ab7a8e0037c241ff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of Fort York Library's\nEntrepreneur in R
 esidence\n(EIR) service.\nHow will having “intercultural communication c
 ompetence” help you in your business? As a newcomer\, you have been expo
 sed to different customs\, norms\, values\, and communication styles. Entr
 epreneur in Residence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, teaches you appropri
 ate and effective words\, tones\, body gestures and facial expressions whe
 n you are negotiating with clients\, vendors\, partners\, employees.\nIn t
 his session:\nAdapt your communication in a language that others can under
 stand.\nDisplay more respect\, patience\, and sensitivity to others’ fee
 lings and needs.\nLearn how managing multicultural teams makes you a more 
 effective leader.\nCome early to network from 6-6:30pm!\nTo apply for one-
 on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Jean\, please fill o
 ut the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n.\nInformation Collection No
 tice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto P
 ublic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, an
 d 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles you
 r information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad774ab7a8e0037c241ff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
