DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T150000
UID:6abe9f27377296003a48f0e0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Become easier to find\, trust\, remember and recommend\nExplor
 e professional reputation\, LinkedIn visibility and authentic relationship
  building. Participants refine how they explain their strengths and what t
 hey want to be known for. Participant takeaway: An improved LinkedIn head
 line\, positioning statement and visibility plan.\nThis is an in person-ev
 ent and takes place at the North York Central library branch.\nQuestions r
 egarding the event can be emailed to ccir@tpl.ca\nThis program is part of 
 TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead 
 donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada\, Fr
 iends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\nThe William and Nona 
 Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careercoa
 ch
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe9f27377296003a48f0e0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
