SUMMARY: WANTON LEE
DESCRIPTION:WANTON LEE — Black Jazz History Comes Alive On Stage!\n\nPres
 ented by Things Falling Apart Theatre\, Wanton Lee is a powerful\, semi-f
 ictional\, soul-stirring theatrical journey inspired by the life\, music 
 and untimely death of legendary jazz trumpeter Lee Morgan.\n\nThrough a d
 ynamic solo performance by Drae Walsh\, audiences are transported into th
 e world of jazz and the complicated life behind the trumpet. Wanton Lee e
 xplores brilliance\, struggle\, love\, addiction\, redemption and the pri
 ce of genius\, revealing the humanity behind one of jazz music’s most ext
 raordinary figures.\n\nFollowing its Toronto engagement in July\, Wanton 
 Lee returns November 30–December 6\, 2026\, at Red Sandcastle Theatre\, 9
 22 Queen Street East\, Toronto.\n\nWritten and Directed by Tien Providenc
 e\nPerformance by Drae Walsh\n\nWhether you're a lifelong jazz lover\, a 
 theatre enthusiast\, a Black history buff\, or simply looking for a compe
 lling Toronto cultural experience\, Wanton Lee offers an unforgettable ev
 ening of storytelling.\n\n🎺 The music. The struggle. The genius. The man
  behind the trumpet.\n\nLive Theatre. Live History.
CATEGORIES:Dance---Performance---Theatre,Red-Sandcastle-Theatre,Storytell
 ing,Concert
