SUMMARY:Writer’s Collective of Canada (WCC): Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T200000
UID:6ae4fc01901b02002cc63eb3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space! A Writers Collective of Canada (WCC) workshop is unlike any other.
  We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, li
 sten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into you
 r story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, an
 d respect. No experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials are pr
 ovided. Workshops are not sequential\; every workshop is unique – join i
 n at any session and let’s write together!\nPresented by Writers Collect
 ive of Canada (WCC)\, a charitable arts-health organization that ignites c
 onnection through creativity by inspiring powerful\, authentic stories sha
 red in community.\nhttps://wcc-cec.org/\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae4fc01901b02002cc63eb3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de5e272866a5b4884877f3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Short Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T193000
UID:69de5e272866a5b4884877f3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in joining a book club but are short on tim
 e?  Then join our Short Book Club\, where we read titles that are 250 page
 s or less. Meetings are held on the second Wednesday of each month.\nOur D
 ecember book is\nSmall Things Like These\nby Claire Keegan\nSummary: It i
 s 1985 in a small Irish town. During the weeks leading up to Christmas\, B
 ill Furlong\, a coal merchant and family man faces into his busiest season
 . Early one morning\, while delivering an order to the local convent\, Bil
 l makes a discovery which forces him to confront both his past and the com
 plicit silences of a town controlled by the church. Already a bestseller i
 n France and certain to be read worldwide for generations to come\, Small 
 Things Like These is a deeply affecting story of hope\, quiet heroism\, an
 d empathy from one of our most critically lauded and iconic writers\nNew m
 embers are most welcome! Please inquire at the circulation desk if you wou
 ld like a copy of the book.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de5e272866a5b4884877f3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f69d42dac6e003721f7fa"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:High Park Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T200000
UID:6a8f69d42dac6e003721f7fa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come and join us on the second Wednesday of every month to dis
 cuss a variety of books.\nEveryone is welcome! Drop-in\, no registration r
 equired.\n2026 Reading List:\nJanuary 14:\nWhat I Mean to Say\n: Remaking 
 Conversation in Our Time by Ian Williams\nFebruary 11:\nFahrenheit 451\nby
  Ray Bradbury\nMarch 11:\nThe Remains of the Day\nby Kazuo Ishiguro\nApril
  8:\nOrbital\nby Samantha Harvey\nMay 13:\nThe Empusium\n: A Health Resort
  Horror Story by Olga Tokarczuk\nJune 10:\nTruth Telling\nSeven Conversati
 ons About Indigenous Life in Canada by Michelle Good\nJuly 8:\nThree Days 
 in June\nby Anne Tyler\nAugust 12:\nThe Woman in the Library\nby Sulari Ge
 ntill\nSeptember 9:\nValentine in Montreal\nby Heather O'Neill\nOctober 14
 :\nOn Tyranny: Twenty Lessons from the Twentieth Century\nby Timothy Snyde
 r\nNovember 11:\nFive Tuesdays in Winter\nby Lily King\nDecember 9: Best B
 ooks of the Year Discussion
LOCATION:High Park\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f69d42dac6e003721f7fa
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
