DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T143000
UID:6ac514a4de300e004518948c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This session will help participants build confidence and prepa
 re for every stage of the interview process. Participants will learn what 
 to expect in pre-interviews\, practice answering interview questions using
  AI tools\, and develop strategies for presenting themselves professionall
 y during video interviews. They will also learn how to use the STAR method
  to provide strong\, structured responses\, navigate inappropriate or ille
 gal interview questions with professionalism\, and understand the value of
  sending post-interview follow-up emails to leave a positive impression.\n
 This workshop is presented by ACCES Employment Toronto\, focused on suppor
 ting jobseekers and employers with a variety of specialized programs and r
 esources both in-person and online.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe p
 ersonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Librar
 y under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The
  information will only be used for event and program registration\, delive
 ry and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informatio
 n can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-59
 81\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac514a4de300e004518948c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
