SUMMARY:Altered Book Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T190000
UID:6ae0df759d27a0004553ad93@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this Altered Book Workshop\, we’ll take old\, discarded b
 ooks\, then transform them into a fun art project! Using the existing page
 s\, we’ll create pockets\, windows\, doors\, secret compartments\, & mo
 re.\nLearn fun techniques for altering books! Take home a project you can 
 continue working on long after the workshop ends.\nNo experience necessary
 \, all are welcome! This is a workshop for teens/youth.\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae0df759d27a0004553ad93
