X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Boardgamestoronto": "https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/events/lkzlztyjcqbxb/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_boardgamestoronto
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Board Games and Social
UID:event_lkzlztyjcqbxb@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261031T052743Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261218T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261218T213000
SUMMARY:Casual Board Games and Pub Social After
DESCRIPTION:Board Games and Social\nThe Board Games event is a fun\, socia
 ble and charitable event\n\nWe are a fun\, friendly and kind group of peop
 le mostly in our 20s\, 30s and 40s. Beginners are welcome! We are a very i
 nclusive and social group and we teach people how to play games they have 
 not played before :)\n\nWe provide a variety of 40+ board games. The games
  usually take 5 or 10 minutes to learn and 30 to 60 minutes to play.\n\nPl
 ay in French: On the last Friday of the month\, we're offering a table whe
 re the games are played in French. Anyone with an intermediate level of Fr
 ench who wants to practice while playing is welcome to join. Just ask for 
 Philippe when you arrive.\n\n**Time**\n\n*Board Games Start time: 630pm\n-
  Board Games end time: 10pm\n*Eat / Drink/ Socialise at a nearby pub after
 wards\n\n**Location**\n\n30 Leeds St\, Toronto\, ON M6G 3R8 (Ukrainian Cat
 holic Church of the Holy Protection)\n\nThe entrance to the board game roo
 m is at the back of the Church. There is a sign on the door that says BOAR
 D GAMES GROUP.\n\nPlease use the map provided on the event page also.\n\nP
 ayment\n**There are two ways to pay**\n**10 by Cash - coins are not accept
 ed. Only bills.****\n**11.55 by Debit/Credit card\n\n**Charity Donations**
 \n\n- This is a not-for-profit initiative. Revenue go towards covering cos
 ts of the event including venue\, insurance marketing\, refreshments and b
 oard games. Any surplus revenue is donated to charity\n\n**Food and drink*
 *\n\n*Everyone will get cookies/candy for free\n- Cups will be provided fo
 r tap water\n*Bring your own food and drink.\n- Please do not bring CHIPS 
 AND CRACKERS as they make a mess and are greasy\n***ALCOHOL IS PROHIBITED 
 AND WE HAVE A ZERO TOLERANCE POLICY ON THIS - there are no second chances*
 *\n\nPhotos will be taken at the event and posted publicly for marketing p
 urposes. Please only attend if you are ok with this or tell me when you ar
 rive that you do not want to be in any photos\n\nThe event is officially h
 osted by Ace of Math Learning Program Ontario Inc.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/events/lkzlztyjcqbx
 b/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260724T174529Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260724T174529Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6962837f91e4576f847bd106"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Between the Lines Bookclub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261218T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261218T200000
UID:6962837f91e4576f847bd106@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Due to renovations the Bookclub will take place in Scadding Co
 urt Community Center in Room 4 (same building)\, participants will be resp
 onsible in sourcing copies of the monthly titles themselves as the branch
  will not be open to the public during this time. We apologize for the inc
 onvenience!\nBecome a page-turner by joining the Between the Lines Book Cl
 ub! Here\, we embark on a new chapter with every read\, diving into a worl
 d of endless possibilities. From gripping thrillers to heartwarming coming
 -of-age tales\, or a sprinkle of fantasy adventures\, there's something fo
 r everyone. Whether you're a die-hard fan of one genre or love mixing thin
 gs up\, you'll find a place here to discuss\, share\, and connect with fel
 low readers. Ready to explore different worlds and discover your next favo
 rite book? Join us and let's turn the page together!\nFriday November 16: 
 A Gentleman in Moscow by Amor Towles\nSet in Moscow in 1922\,\nA Gentlem
 an in Moscow\nby Amor Towles follows Count Alexander Rostov\, a refined Ru
 ssian aristocrat sentenced by a Bolshevik tribunal to house arrest in the 
 grand Metropol Hotel\, where he must spend the rest of his life confined w
 ithin its walls. As the world outside undergoes dramatic political and soc
 ial change\, the Count gradually transforms his restricted circumstances i
 nto a life rich with unexpected friendships\, meaningful encounters\, and 
 quiet adventures. From navigating the hotel's intricate social world to fo
 rming a particularly meaningful bond with a young girl named Nina\, Rostov
  discovers new perspectives on love\, loyalty\, personal growth\, and the 
 passage of time. Elegant\, witty\, and deeply moving\, the novel explores 
 the nature of freedom\, the importance of human connection\, and the possi
 bility of finding purpose and beauty even when life takes an unexpected tu
 rn.
LOCATION:Sanderson - Closed\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6962837f91e4576f847bd106
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
