SUMMARY:Pokémon TCG Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261228T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261228T190000
UID:6a7b47a3c80d09476c940401@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Grab your cards and get your decks ready for a fun-filled Pok
 émon TCG experience! Whether you are a seasoned Trainer or new to the gam
 e\, come explore the world of Pokémon\, learn how to play the trading car
 d game\, discover the newest cards and sets\, and enjoy friendly matches w
 ith other trainers.\nFor ages 8-12 only (Younger siblings are welcome to a
 ttend with a caregiver\; quiet activities such as coloring may be provided
 )\n*For all registered Children's programs at Malvern\, there is a grace p
 eriod of 10 minutes. After the first 10 minutes of a program\, spots will 
 be given to waiting customers.*\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7b47a3c80d09476c940401
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae3698debad22004548d23f"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Festival Select: Sorcerer (William Friedkin\, 1977)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261228T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261228T203000
UID:6ae3698debad22004548d23f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join the Society and Recreation department of the North York C
 entral Library for monthly screenings of fiction and non-fiction films tha
 t push the boundaries of the medium. This month we are showing William Fri
 edkin's\nSorcerer\n(1977).\nSynopsis (The Criterion Collection): A halluc
 inatory journey into the heart of darkness\, William Friedkin’s pulse-po
 unding reimagining of the suspense classic\nThe Wages of Fear\nwas dismiss
 ed upon its release\, only to be recognized decades later as one of the Ne
 w Hollywood’s boldest auteur statements. In a remote Latin American vill
 age\, four desperate fugitives—a New Jersey gangster (Roy Scheider)\, a 
 Mexican assassin (Francisco Rabal)\, an unscrupulous Parisian businessman 
 (Bruno Cremer)\, and an Arab terrorist (Amidou)—take on a doomed mission
 : transporting two trucks full of highly explosive nitroglycerin through t
 he treacherous jungle. Aided by Tangerine Dream’s otherworldly synth sco
 re\, Friedkin turns each bump in the road into a tour de force of cold-swe
 at tension—conjuring a hauntingly nihilistic vision of a world ruled by 
 chance and fate.\nNo registration required.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae3698debad22004548d23f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
