DESCRIPTION:Do you love reading and talking about books?  Join us for an i
 nformal\, relaxed\, and casual meeting to discuss various books throughout
  the year.  The book club will meet monthly on the following dates:\nJan 2
 0:                   In The Upper Country\nby Kai Thomas\nFeb 17:         
           Complicated Kindness\nby Miriam Toews\nMarch 17:             Ful
 l Disclosure\nby Beverly McLachlin\nApril 21:                Half of a Yel
 low Sun\nby Chimamanda Adichie\nMay 19:                 Great Along\nby Kr
 istin Hannah\nJune 16:                 Tell the Wolves\nI’m Home\nby Kar
 a Rifka Brunt\nJuly 21:                  Cold Mountain\nby Charles Frazier
 \nAugust 18: A Great Country\nby Gowda Somaya\nSeptember 15: How to Say Ba
 bylon\nby Safiya Sinclair\nOctober 20: Crying in H Mart: a memoir\nby Mich
 elle Zauner\nNovember 17: Educated\nby Tara Westover\nDecember 15: Horse\n
 by Geraldine Brooks\nDrop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Evelyn Gregory
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abfe5aa29c3d600332d325e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
