BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/challenging-biases-in-decision-making-and-approaches-to-difference-biases-in-decision-making/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Challenging Biases in Decision Making and Approaches to Difference
  (Biases in Decision Making)
DTSTART:20270125T180000Z
DTEND:20270125T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260923T184100Z
UID:MEC-1f3a4f7715b9fd855595b4836101ec30@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20270125T180000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp\; Inclusion,Equity, People &amp\; Cultur
 e
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260923
DESCRIPTION:In Challenging Biases in Decision-Making and Approaches to Dif
 ference\, participants will learn about how our brains develop and rely on
  biases\, how these biases impact our perceptions and behaviours\, and wha
 t we can do to prevent these biases from influencing our decisions\, workp
 laces\, and communities. This session will consider how biases can affect 
 the systems we work within and offer some opportunities to consider how to
  remove the opportunity for bias within our systems.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923
LOCATION:https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?i
 d=1396
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/challenging-biases-in-decision-making-a
 nd-approaches-to-difference-biases-in-decision-making/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab5a6473dd190003e746a27"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Screen Scaries
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270125T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270125T200000
UID:6ab5a6473dd190003e746a27@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Get your spook on with this month's scary movie screening of\
 nSuspiria\n(1977)\, directed by Dario Argento.\nThis dreamy\, psychotronic
  Gothic from Italian horror-master Argento follows a new student as she en
 ters a prestigious ballet academy\, where she is troubled by strange and s
 inister goings-on behind the institution's walls.\nSuspiria\nhas a running
  time of 1 hour and 32 minutes\, and is rated 18A.\nThere will be a short 
 introduction to the film followed by the screening\, which will be accompa
 nied by closed captions.\nThe next Screen Scaries will be:\nDecember 28\, 
 2026:\nBlack Christmas\n(1974\, USA) Bob Clark. Runtime: 1h37m\; Rating: R
 \nJanuary 25\, 2027:\nRing\n(1998\, Japan) Hideo Nakata. Runtime: 1h35m\; 
 Rating: PG
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab5a6473dd190003e746a27
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
