DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270311T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270311T170000
DTSTAMP:20261009T163950Z
CREATED:20261009T162424Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261009T163950Z
UID:36032-1804777200-1804784400@philosophy.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Colloquium (Ram Neta\, University of North Carolina)
DESCRIPTION:The Department is pleased to welcome Ram Neta\, a professor in the Department of Philosophy\, at Harvard University for a colloquium on April 1\, 2027. He specializes in epistemology and is currently at work on a book on the nature of knowledge. In particular\, he is trying to understand what knowledge is by examining the various ways in which knowing some things depends upon knowing other things. \nTitle\nTBD \nAbstract\nTBD
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/colloquium-ram-neta-university-of-north-carolina/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building 100
CATEGORIES:Alumni,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/avif:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Neta-150x150-1-148x150-1.avif
END:VEVENT
